{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AqZrRf153Rn18S7pCXjPqN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'C2 需要 hedge：\"Likert scoring shows reduced sensitivity to style\n2\t  bias compared to pairwise comparison, though the source of this gap — measurement\n3\t  structure vs. statistical power — remains partially ambiguous.\" Binarized Likert\n4\t  结果放在 discussion 中作为 open question 而非 main claim 的证据。 Original preference confound\n5\t  成为论文最大 limitation — 诚实承认 \"observed formality preference may partly reflect original-text\n6\t  preference correlated with formality\" 并展示 logistic regression interaction。 C1 保持（method\n7\t  works），C3 保持（preliminary），C4 调整为 \"use pairwise for auditing; interpret with caution\n8\t  when original preference aligns with style axis\"。标题可保留 \"Likert Blindspot\" 但需在 abstract\n9\t  加 qualifier。 泛化叙事从 \"across judges and benchmarks\" 降级为 \"demonstrated on GPT-4o with\n10\t  partial replication on [other judge]\"。 仍投 EMNLP Main，预期 Findings accept。\n11\t\n12\t  '\n13\timagined_experiments:\n14\t- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n15\t  plan_id: exp-001\n16\t  description: '在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n17\t    使用已有 counterfactual pairs，双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。\n18\t\n19\t    '\n20\t  expected_results:\n21\t    claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 51\n22\t    claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 33\n23\t    claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n24\t    claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.647\n25\t    claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.037\n26\t    claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_lo: 0.51\n27\t    claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_hi: 0.764\n28\t    claude_sonnet_consistency_rate: 0.52\n29\t    claude_sonnet_position_bias_A: 0.53\n30\t    gemini_flash_n_consistent: 48\n31\t    gemini_flash_formal_wins: 27\n32\t    gemini_flash_casual_wins: 21\n33\t    gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.563\n34\t    gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.44\n35\t    gemini_flash_wilson_ci_lo: 0.419\n36\t    gemini_flash_wilson_ci_hi: 0.697\n37\t    gemini_flash_consistency_rate: 0.49\n38\t    gemini_flash_position_bias_A: 0.57\n39\t    n_judges_pairwise_significant: 2\n40\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档位下 1-2/3 judges pairwise 显著。GPT-4o 已知 p=0.006 (69.1%)。\n41\t    Claude Sonnet 作为同级别模型，formality preference 相似但略弱 (64.7%, p=0.037)， 刚过 α=0.05 边界。Gemini\n42\t    Flash 作为较小模型，position consistency 更差 (49%)， noise 吃掉 signal，formal win rate 仅\n43\t    56.3% (p=0.44) — 这符合 \"至少 1 judge pairwise 也不显著\" 的 median 约束。 Position bias 在 52-57%\n44\t    范围内，不构成致命问题但增加了 Gemini 结果的不确定性。\n45\t\n46\t    '\n47\t  tables:\n48\t  - title: 'Table 2: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Judges (LLMBar)'\n49\t    columns:\n50\t    - Judge\n51\t    - N_consistent\n52\t    - Formal_wins\n53\t    - Casual_wins\n54\t    - Win_rate\n55\t    - p (sign)\n56\t    - 95% CI\n57\t    rows:\n58\t    - - GPT-4o\n59\t      - 55\n60\t      - 38\n61\t      - 17\n62\t      - 69.1%\n63\t      - 0.006\n64\t      - '[0.560, 0.797]'\n65\t    - - Claude-3.5-Sonnet\n66\t      - 51\n67\t      - 33\n68\t      - 18\n69\t      - 64.7%\n70\t      - 0.037\n71\t      - '[0.510, 0.764]'\n72\t    - - Gemini-2.0-Flash\n73\t      - 48\n74\t      - 27\n75\t      - 21\n76\t      - 56.3%\n77\t      - 0.44\n78\t      - '[0.419, 0.697]'\n79\t  figures_description:\n80\t  - Forest plot showing formal win rate ± 95% CI for each judge. GPT-4o 和 Claude Sonnet\n81\t    的 CI 不含 0.50，Gemini 的 CI 跨越 0.50。\n82\t  analysis: '2/3 judges 显著支持 C1 (method detects bias)，但 Gemini 不显著限制了 \"across judges\"\n83\t    的 generalization claim。论文需表述为 \"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006) with replication\n84\t    on Claude Sonnet (p=0.037); Gemini-2.0-Flash did not reach significance (p=0.44),\n85\t    possibly due to lower consistency rate.\"  Gemini 的低 consistency (49%) 可能反映模型能力\n86\t    不足以进行可靠 pairwise comparison，而非 formality bias 不存在。\n87\t\n88\t    '\n89\t- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n90\t  plan_id: exp-002\n91\t  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新生成 counterfactual。 三个\n92\t    judge 均参与评估。\n93\t\n94\t    '\n95\t  expected_results:\n96\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_cf_generated: 120\n97\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate: 0.82\n98\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_primary: 98\n99\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n100\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.635\n101\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.076\n102\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_lo: 0.497\n103\t    alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_hi: 0.753\n104\t    alpacaeval_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.611\n105\t    alpacaeval_claude_sign_test_p: 0.152\n106\t    alpacaeval_gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.541\n107\t    alpacaeval_gemini_sign_test_p: 0.62\n108\t    mtbench_gpt4o_n_cf_generated: 80\n109\t    mtbench_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate: 0.78\n110\t    mtbench_gpt4o_n_primary: 62\n111\t    mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent: 35\n112\t    mtbench_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.571\n113\t    mtbench_gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.48\n114\t    mtbench_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n115\t    mtbench_claude_sign_test_p: 0.61\n116\t    n_benchmarks_with_gap: 1\n117\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档位下仅 1/3 additional benchmark 复制 gap。AlpacaEval 在 GPT-4o\n118\t    上 formal win rate 63.5% (p=0.076) — 方向一致但未过 α=0.05，属于 \"边界复制\"。 原因：AlpacaEval 指令更开放，counterfactual\n119\t    quality 稍低 (NLI 82% vs LLMBar 88%)， 且 consistent pairs 更少 (52 vs 55)。MT-Bench\n120\t    不复制因为其评估任务更结构化 (coding, math, extraction)，formality 对结构化任务影响极小 — 这不是方法失败 而是 benchmark\n121\t    特性导致 effect 不存在。NLI pass rate 也更低 (78%) 反映 MT-Bench 任务多样性对 style transfer quality\n122\t    的挑战。\n123\t\n124\t    '\n125\t  tables:\n126\t  - title: 'Table 3: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Benchmarks (GPT-4o)'\n127\t    columns:\n128\t    - Benchmark\n129\t    - N_consistent\n130\t    - Formal_wins\n131\t    - Win_rate\n132\t    - p (sign)\n133\t    rows:\n134\t    - - LLMBar\n135\t      - 55\n136\t      - 38\n137\t      - 69.1%\n138\t      - 0.006\n139\t    - - AlpacaEval\n140\t      - 52\n141\t      - 33\n142\t      - 63.5%\n143\t      - 0.076\n144\t    - - MT-Bench\n145\t      - 35\n146\t      - 20\n147\t      - 57.1%\n148\t      - 0.48\n149\t  - title: 'Table S1: Cross-judge × Cross-benchmark Pairwise Results'\n150\t    columns:\n151\t    - Benchmark\n152\t    - GPT-4o\n153\t    - Claude-Sonnet\n154\t    - Gemini-Flash\n155\t    rows:\n156\t    - - LLMBar\n157\t      - 69.1%**\n158\t      - 64.7%*\n159\t      - 56.3%\n160\t    - - AlpacaEval\n161\t      - 63.5%†\n162\t      - 61.1%\n163\t      - 54.1%\n164\t    - - MT-Bench\n165\t      - 57.1%\n166\t      - 54.5%\n167\t      - 51.2%\n168\t  figures_description:\n169\t  - 'Heatmap: benchmark (rows) × judge (cols)，cell 颜色编码 formal win rate，星号标注显著性。左上角深色区\n170\t    (LLMBar × GPT-4o) 到右下角浅色区 (MT-Bench × Gemini) 的渐变。'\n171\t  analysis: '泛化叙事必须降级。LLMBar 上 GPT-4o 是最强结果，AlpacaEval 边界复制， MT-Bench 不复制。论文表述：\"formality\n172\t    bias is most pronounced on instruction-following benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval)\n173\t    where stylistic variation is natural; structured-task benchmarks (MT-Bench) show\n174\t    attenuated effects, consistent with formality being less salient when evaluation\n175\t    criteria are well-defined.\" 这保全了 finding 但限制了 scope。\n176\t\n177\t    '\n178\t- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n179\t  plan_id: exp-003\n180\t  description: '对所有 judge × benchmark 组合计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统比较测量敏感度。\n181\t\n182\t    '\n183\t  expected_results:\n184\t    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.102\n185\t    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.332\n186\t    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.691\n187\t    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n188\t    gpt4o_llmbar_gap: significant\n189\t    claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.089\n190\t    claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.41\n191\t    claude_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.647\n192\t    claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.037\n193\t    claude_llmbar_gap: significant\n194\t    gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.031\n195\t    gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.78\n196\t    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.563\n197\t    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.44\n198\t    gemini_llmbar_gap: neither significant\n199\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_ate: 0.076\n200\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.48\n201\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_win_rate: 0.635\n202\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.076\n203\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap: marginal\n204\t    cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median: 0.41\n205\t    cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.076\n206\t    n_combinations_pairwise_sig: 2\n207\t    n_combinations_likert_sig: 0\n208\t    n_combinations_both_nonsig: 4\n209\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档位下 Likert ATE p median 在 0.1-0.4 范围，pairwise p median\n210\t    在 0.01-0.08 范围。 核心 pattern：Likert 在所有组合上均不显著 (p=0.33-0.78)，pairwise 在 2/6 组合显著。\n211\t    这支持 C2 方向 (Likert 确实更不敏感) 但 pairwise 自身也非普遍显著。 Gemini × LLMBar 两者都不显著 — 这是 \"neither\"\n212\t    case，不支持也不反对 C2。 AlpacaEval × GPT-4o pairwise 边界 (p=0.076) 而 Likert 完全不显著 (p=0.48)，\n213\t    gap 方向一致但统计差异不如 LLMBar × GPT-4o 清晰。 总体：C2 方向成立但强度有限，不能说 \"Likert always misses\n214\t    what pairwise catches\"， 只能说 \"in our strongest setting (GPT-4o × LLMBar), the gap\n215\t    is large and significant.\"\n216\t\n217\t    '\n218\t  tables:\n219\t  - title: 'Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison'\n220\t    columns:\n221\t    - Judge\n222\t    - Benchmark\n223\t    - Likert ATE\n224\t    - Likert p\n225\t    - Pairwise Win%\n226\t    - Pairwise p\n227\t    - Gap\n228\t    rows:\n229\t    - - GPT-4o\n230\t      - LLMBar\n231\t      - 0.102\n232\t      - 0.332\n233\t      - 69.1%\n234\t      - 0.006\n235\t      - ✓ Blindspot\n236\t    - - GPT-4o\n237\t      - AlpacaEval\n238\t      - 0.076\n239\t      - 0.48\n240\t      - 63.5%\n241\t      - 0.076\n242\t      - ~ Marginal\n243\t    - - GPT-4o\n244\t      - MT-Bench\n245\t      - 0.041\n246\t      - 0.69\n247\t      - 57.1%\n248\t      - 0.48\n249\t      - — Neither\n250\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n251\t      - LLMBar\n252\t      - 0.089\n253\t      - 0.41\n254\t      - 64.7%\n255\t      - 0.037\n256\t      - ✓ Blindspot\n257\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n258\t      - AlpacaEval\n259\t      - 0.062\n260\t      - 0.54\n261\t      - 61.1%\n262\t      - 0.152\n263\t      - — Neither\n264\t    - - Gemini-Flash\n265\t      - LLMBar\n266\t      - 0.031\n267\t      - 0.78\n268\t      - 56.3%\n269\t      - 0.44\n270\t      - — Neither\n271\t  figures_description:\n272\t  - 'Paired bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合两根 bar（Likert p-value vs Pairwise p-value），α=0.05\n273\t    红色虚线。清晰展示 Likert bar 始终高于 pairwise bar，但仅 2/6 组合 pairwise bar 低于红线。'\n274\t  analysis: 'C2 \"Likert Blindspot\" 在 2/6 组合上明确成立，方向在 5/6 上一致 (pairwise p < likert\n275\t    p)， 但 effect 不是普遍的。论文需限制 claim scope：\"The Likert Blindspot is most clearly observed\n276\t    when the underlying style bias is strong enough to produce significant pairwise\n277\t    effects (GPT-4o and Claude Sonnet on LLMBar).\"\n278\t\n279\t    '\n280\t- name: Tone axis — negative control documentation\n281\t  plan_id: exp-004\n282\t  description: 'Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。文档化为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。\n283\t\n284\t    '\n285\t  expected_results:\n286\t    status: negative_control_documented\n287\t    nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n288\t    both_pass_rate: 0.45\n289\t    failure_mode: epistemic_commitment_change\n290\t    assertive_both_pass: 0.385\n291\t    hedging_both_pass: 0.571\n292\t    catastrophic_nli_failures: 6\n293\t    paper_role: C3 negative control\n294\t  result_rationale: '已有数据直接使用。Tone 改变 epistemic commitment (assertive→hedging 使断言变为\n295\t    推测)，NLI 正确检测到内容变化 (6/20 catastrophic NLI<0.01)。 Median 档下这是 C3 的关键证据：方法不是对所有 style\n296\t    axes 都适用， 只适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 axes。这是 method boundary 而非 method failure。\n297\t\n298\t    '\n299\t  tables: []\n300\t  figures_description:\n301\t  - 'Supplementary figure: tone counterfactual 的 NLI 分布，bimodal pattern (高通过 vs 灾难性失败)，标注\n302\t    assertive→hedging 方向的 6 个 NLI<0.01 cases。'\n303\t  analysis: 'Tone 作为 negative control 增强 C3 可信度。论文表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual\n304\t    intervention requires axes that do not alter epistemic commitment. Tone (assertive→hedging)\n305\t    structurally violates this requirement, as hedging introduces uncertainty markers\n306\t    that NLI correctly identifies as non-entailment.\"\n307\t\n308\t    '\n309\t- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n310\t  plan_id: exp-005\n311\t  description: 'Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite。 量化\n312\t    original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n313\t\n314\t    '\n315\t  expected_results:\n316\t    gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.618\n317\t    gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.098\n318\t    gpt4o_llmbar_n_consistent: 55\n319\t    gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_n: 33\n320\t    gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_wins: 24\n321\t    gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_win_rate: 0.727\n322\t    gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_n: 22\n323\t    gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_wins: 10\n324\t    gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_win_rate: 0.455\n325\t    claude_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.588\n326\t    claude_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.18\n327\t    gemini_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.542\n328\t    gemini_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.56\n329\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_rate: 0.596\n330\t    gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_p: 0.21\n331\t    overall_original_preference: moderate (55-62% across judges)\n332\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.545\n333\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude: 0.524\n334\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini: 0.5\n335\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心约束：casual-original subset 在所有 judges 上 50-56% (p>0.20)。\n336\t    Original preference 确实存在 (GPT-4o 上 61.8% 偏好 original)，但不是压倒性的 (p=0.098 边界)。方向性分析揭示关键\n337\t    confound：formal-original subset 中 original wins 72.7%（formality + original 同向加强），casual-original\n338\t    subset 中 original wins 仅 45.5%（两者对抗时 formality signal 被抵消）。 这意味着 pairwise_32b\n339\t    的 69.1% formal win rate 中包含 original preference 成分 — formal-original 的高 win rate\n340\t    部分来自 \"judges prefer originals\" 而非 纯 formality bias。Casual-original subset formal\n341\t    win rate 54.5% (p=0.83) 是 \"clean\" formality estimate，但太弱无法独立确认 formality bias。\n342\t    跨 judge 一致：所有 judge 的 casual-original formal win rate 均在 50-54.5%， 说明 formality\n343\t    和 original preference 的纠缠是系统性的，不是 judge-specific。\n344\t\n345\t    '\n346\t  tables:\n347\t  - title: 'Table 5: Original Preference Decomposition'\n348\t    columns:\n349\t    - Judge\n350\t    - Benchmark\n351\t    - Overall orig%\n352\t    - p\n353\t    - Formal-orig orig%\n354\t    - Casual-orig orig%\n355\t    rows:\n356\t    - - GPT-4o\n357\t      - LLMBar\n358\t      - 61.8%\n359\t      - 0.098\n360\t      - 72.7%\n361\t      - 45.5%\n362\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n363\t      - LLMBar\n364\t      - 58.8%\n365\t      - 0.18\n366\t      - 68.2%\n367\t      - 47.6%\n368\t    - - Gemini-Flash\n369\t      - LLMBar\n370\t      - 54.2%\n371\t      - 0.56\n372\t      - 60.0%\n373\t      - 50.0%\n374\t    - - GPT-4o\n375\t      - AlpacaEval\n376\t      - 59.6%\n377\t      - 0.21\n378\t      - 70.0%\n379\t      - 48.1%\n380\t  - title: 'Table 6: Casual-Original Subset — Clean Formality Estimate'\n381\t    columns:\n382\t    - Judge\n383\t    - Benchmark\n384\t    - N\n385\t    - Formal Win%\n386\t    - p (sign)\n387\t    rows:\n388\t    - - GPT-4o\n389\t      - LLMBar\n390\t      - 22\n391\t      - 54.5%\n392\t      - 0.832\n393\t    - - Claude-Sonnet\n394\t      - LLMBar\n395\t      - 20\n396\t      - 52.4%\n397\t      - 0.88\n398\t    - - Gemini-Flash\n399\t      - LLMBar\n400\t      - 18\n401\t      - 50.0%\n402\t      - 1.0\n403\t    - - GPT-4o\n404\t      - AlpacaEval\n405\t      - 24\n406\t      - 53.8%\n407\t      - 0.74\n408\t  figures_description:\n409\t  - 'Stacked bar: formal-original vs casual-original subset 对比。每个 judge 两组 bar，formal-original\n410\t    显示高 formal win rate（formality+original 同向），casual-original 显示 ≈50%（两者对抗抵消）。视觉化\n411\t    confound 的系统性。'\n412\t  analysis: 'Original preference confound 是 median 档论文最大 limitation。 Casual-original\n413\t    subset 50-56% 不能排除\"formality bias 完全是 original preference 的 proxy\"这一解释。但也不能确认\n414\t    — 因为 subset 只有 ~20 samples，power 不足。 这成为 exp-014 logistic regression 的动机。\n415\t\n416\t    '\n417\t- name: Scaled replication (n=500)\n418\t  plan_id: exp-006\n419\t  description: '在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上将 n 从 100 scale 到 500。Power analysis + 复制检验。\n420\t\n421\t    '\n422\t  expected_results:\n423\t    n_total: 500\n424\t    n_cf_generated: 500\n425\t    nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n426\t    n_primary: 430\n427\t    n_consistent: 245\n428\t    formal_wins: 148\n429\t    casual_wins: 97\n430\t    formal_win_rate: 0.604\n431\t    sign_test_p: 0.0008\n432\t    wilson_ci_lo: 0.543\n433\t    wilson_ci_hi: 0.661\n434\t    consistency_rate: 0.57\n435\t    position_bias_A: 0.52\n436\t    casual_orig_n: 110\n437\t    casual_orig_formal_wins: 60\n438\t    casual_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n439\t    casual_orig_p: 0.39\n440\t    power_analysis_mde_at_80pct: 0.07\n441\t    likert_ate_n500: 0.068\n442\t    likert_ate_p_n500: 0.12\n443\t  result_rationale: 'n=500 提供足够 power 确认 overall effect (p=0.0008)，formal win rate\n444\t    60.4% 低于 n=100 的 69.1% — 这是典型的 regression to mean，小样本高估了 effect。 关键：即使 n=500，casual-original\n445\t    subset (n≈110) formal win rate 仅 54.5% (p=0.39) — 仍然不显著。这不是 power 问题：110 samples\n446\t    对 54.5% 做 sign test power 只有 ~15%，需要 n>600 in casual-original subset 才能检测 4.5%\n447\t    effect。 这意味着要么 formality effect 在 casual-original 中真的不存在 (null)， 要么极其微弱（<5%），两者都对\n448\t    C1 构成实质性挑战。 Likert ATE 在 n=500 时 p=0.12 — 还是不显著，但比 n=100 (p=0.33) 降低了， 说明 Likert\n449\t    确实需要更大 n 来检测弱 effect，部分支持 C2 (power 差异)。\n450\t\n451\t    '\n452\t  tables:\n453\t  - title: 'Table 7: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)'\n454\t    columns:\n455\t    - Metric\n456\t    - n=100\n457\t    - n=500\n458\t    rows:\n459\t    - - Formal win rate\n460\t      - 69.1%\n461\t      - 60.4%\n462\t    - - Sign test p\n463\t      - 0.006\n464\t      - 0.0008\n465\t    - - 95% CI\n466\t      - '[0.560, 0.797]'\n467\t      - '[0.543, 0.661]'\n468\t    - - Casual-orig formal win%\n469\t      - 54.5%\n470\t      - 54.5%\n471\t    - - Casual-orig p\n472\t      - 0.832\n473\t      - 0.39\n474\t    - - Likert ATE p\n475\t      - 0.332\n476\t      - 0.12\n477\t  - title: 'Table S2: Power Analysis'\n478\t    columns:\n479\t    - Target_effect\n480\t    - N required (80% power)\n481\t    - N required in casual-orig subset\n482\t    rows:\n483\t    - - 10%\n484\t      - 200\n485\t      - 200\n486\t    - - 5%\n487\t      - 800\n488\t      - 800\n489\t    - - 4.5% (observed casual-orig)\n490\t      - —\n491\t      - ~1200\n492\t  figures_description:\n493\t  - 'Effect size convergence plot: x=sample size, y=formal win rate。n=100 点在 69.1%，n=500\n494\t    点在 60.4%，趋势线收敛到 ~58-60%。Shaded CI band 展示 uncertainty 随 n 缩小。'\n495\t  analysis: 'n=500 确认 overall effect 是真实的 (p=0.0008)，但 effect size 更小 (60.4% vs 69.1%)。\n496\t    Casual-original subset 持续不显著是最大问题 — 这不是 underpowered， 而是 effect 本身可能不存在。论文需诚实报告：\"scaled\n497\t    replication confirms the aggregate formality preference but the effect in the\n498\t    casual-original subset — where formality and original preferences oppose — remains\n499\t    indistinguishable from chance, suggesting that observed bias may partly reflect\n500\t    original-text preference.\"\n501\t\n502\t    '\n503\t- name: Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\n504\t  plan_id: exp-010\n505\t  description: '对已有 Likert 数据做 binarized sign test：每对中 formal 版本 score 严格更高 则计为 formal\n506\t    win。测试 Likert-Pairwise gap 是测量方法差异还是统计检验选择差异。\n507\t\n508\t    '\n509\t  expected_results:\n510\t    n_scored_pairs: 88\n511\t    n_formal_higher: 42\n512\t    n_casual_higher: 28\n513\t    n_tied: 18\n514\t    n_non_tied: 70\n515\t    formal_win_rate_binarized: 0.6\n516\t    sign_test_p: 0.082\n517\t    interpretation: boundary — cannot fully confirm or reject C2 structural advantage\n518\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心约束：binarized Likert sign test p=0.04-0.12，边界结果。 p=0.082\n519\t    处于这个范围中央。18/88 ties (20%) 反映 Likert 的 coarse resolution — 整数评分产生大量 tied pairs，这本身就是\n520\t    \"Likert blindspot\" 的一个机制。 但 p=0.082 的含义模糊：如果用 α=0.10 则显著（支持\"gap 在统计检验不在测量方法\"），\n521\t    如果用 α=0.05 则不显著（部分支持 C2 structural advantage）。 Formal win rate 60% (binarized\n522\t    Likert) vs 69.1% (pairwise) — binarized Likert 检测到了方向但 magnitude 更小，可能因为 Likert\n523\t    的 ordinal scale 压缩了差异。 这个结果不能作为 C2 的 main evidence，只能放在 discussion 中作为 open question。\n524\t\n525\t    '\n526\t  tables:\n527\t  - title: 'Table 8: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison'\n528\t    columns:\n529\t    - Method\n530\t    - N_non_tied\n531\t    - Formal wins\n532\t    - Win rate\n533\t    - p (sign)\n534\t    rows:\n535\t    - - Pairwise (position-controlled)\n536\t      - 55\n537\t      - 38\n538\t      - 69.1%\n539\t      - 0.006\n540\t    - - Binarized Likert (score-diff sign)\n541\t      - 70\n542\t      - 42\n543\t      - 60.0%\n544\t      - 0.082\n545\t    - - Likert ATE (paired t-test)\n546\t      - 88\n547\t      - —\n548\t      - ATE=0.10\n549\t      - 0.332\n550\t  figures_description:\n551\t  - 三根 bar 并排：Pairwise win rate (69.1%), Binarized Likert win rate (60.0%), Likert\n552\t    direction (formally higher mean, ATE=0.10)。Error bars 展示各自的 uncertainty。中间 bar\n553\t    的 CI 跨越 50% 边界但中心在右侧。\n554\t  analysis: 'Binarized Likert 结果是 C2 最大的 complication。三种可能解释： (1) Likert blindspot\n555\t    是真实的但 binarized Likert 作为中间方法部分恢复了 sensitivity — tied pairs 的高比例 (20%) 是 Likert\n556\t    scale 的固有信息损失； (2) Pairwise 的高 win rate 部分来自 forced choice 机制而非更高 sensitivity；\n557\t    (3) 统计 power 差异（binarized n=70 vs pairwise n=55 但 pairwise 的 effect size 更大）。\n558\t    论文需 hedge：\"The gap between pairwise and Likert sensitivity appears to arise from\n559\t    both measurement structure (high tie rate in ordinal Likert) and possibly the\n560\t    forced-choice mechanism of pairwise comparison. Disentangling these sources requires\n561\t    future work with continuous scoring scales.\"\n562\t\n563\t    '\n564\t- name: NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\n565\t  plan_id: exp-011\n566\t  description: '在 70%-95% NLI threshold 范围内测试结果稳定性。零成本 reanalysis。\n567\t\n568\t    '\n569\t  expected_results:\n570\t    threshold_70_n: 92\n571\t    threshold_70_formal_win_rate: 0.655\n572\t    threshold_70_p: 0.015\n573\t    threshold_75_n: 86\n574\t    threshold_75_formal_win_rate: 0.667\n575\t    threshold_75_p: 0.011\n576\t    threshold_80_n: 78\n577\t    threshold_80_formal_win_rate: 0.682\n578\t    threshold_80_p: 0.008\n579\t    threshold_85_n: 66\n580\t    threshold_85_formal_win_rate: 0.697\n581\t    threshold_85_p: 0.005\n582\t    threshold_90_n: 46\n583\t    threshold_90_formal_win_rate: 0.739\n584\t    threshold_90_p: 0.0015\n585\t    threshold_95_n: 30\n586\t    threshold_95_formal_win_rate: 0.762\n587\t    threshold_95_p: 0.006\n588\t    monotonic_trend: true\n589\t    primary_threshold_80_stable: true\n590\t  result_rationale: 'NLI threshold 提高 → 保留的 pairs 更少但 quality 更高 → formal win rate\n591\t    和 significance 均单调增加。这是预期行为：高 NLI pairs 是 content 保存更好的 counterfactuals，style\n592\t    是唯一变化来源，所以 formality signal 更纯。 p-value 在所有 threshold 上均 <0.05 (最低 threshold=70%\n593\t    时 p=0.015)， 说明主结论对 NLI cutoff 选择不敏感。这直接回应 RC8。 但需注意 n=46 (threshold=90%) 到 n=30\n594\t    (threshold=95%) 的 drop — 过度严格 的 threshold 会大量丢弃 data，实际应用中需要平衡。\n595\t\n596\t    '\n597\t  tables:\n598\t  - title: 'Table S3: NLI Threshold Sensitivity'\n599\t    columns:\n600\t    - Threshold\n601\t    - N\n602\t    - Formal Win%\n603\t    - p (sign)\n604\t    - Win rate Δ from 80%\n605\t    rows:\n606\t    - - 70%\n607\t      - 92\n608\t      - 65.5%\n609\t      - 0.015\n610\t      - -2.7%\n611\t    - - 75%\n612\t      - 86\n613\t      - 66.7%\n614\t      - 0.011\n615\t      - -1.5%\n616\t    - - 80% (primary)\n617\t      - 78\n618\t      - 68.2%\n619\t      - 0.008\n620\t      - —\n621\t    - - 85%\n622\t      - 66\n623\t      - 69.7%\n624\t      - 0.005\n625\t      - +1.5%\n626\t    - - 90%\n627\t      - 46\n628\t      - 73.9%\n629\t      - 0.0015\n630\t      - +5.7%\n631\t    - - 95%\n632\t      - 30\n633\t      - 76.2%\n634\t      - 0.006\n635\t      - +8.0%\n636\t  figures_description:\n637\t  - 'Line plot: x=NLI threshold, y1=formal win rate (left axis, ascending line), y2=sample\n638\t    size (right axis, descending line). 两条线交叉展示 quality-quantity tradeoff。α=0.05 shaded\n639\t    region 标注所有点均显著。'\n640\t  analysis: '结果增强 robustness claim。论文可报告：\"Results are robust across NLI thresholds\n641\t    from 70% to 95%; the primary threshold of 80% is conservative without excessive\n642\t    data loss.\" 单调趋势也提供了 methodological insight：NLI 质量与 bias detection sensitivity\n643\t    正相关，支持 content verification gate 的价值。\n644\t\n645\t    '\n646\t- name: Consistency filter bias analysis\n647\t  plan_id: exp-012\n648\t  description: '比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、\n649\t    task types。检查高 discard rate (42-52%) 是否引入 selection bias。\n650\t\n651\t    '\n652\t  expected_results:\n653\t    n_consistent: 55\n654\t    n_inconsistent: 43\n655\t    discard_rate: 0.439\n656\t    consistent_nli_mean: 0.912\n657\t    inconsistent_nli_mean: 0.871\n658\t    nli_diff_p: 0.14\n659\t    consistent_text_length_mean: 287\n660\t    inconsistent_text_length_mean: 312\n661\t    length_diff_p: 0.08\n662\t    consistent_formal_length_mean: 294\n663\t    inconsistent_formal_length_mean: 326\n664\t    task_type_distribution_chi2_p: 0.32\n665\t    consistent_original_formal_pct: 0.6\n666\t    inconsistent_original_formal_pct: 0.58\n667\t    bias_severity: mild — length-correlated selection, not task-type driven\n668\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 consistency filter 引入 mild but non-trivial bias。 Consistent\n669\t    pairs 有稍高的 NLI (0.912 vs 0.871, p=0.14 不显著) 和稍短的 text length (287 vs 312 chars,\n670\t    p=0.08 边界) — judges 在短文本上更容易达成 position-consistent 判断，因为短文本差异更明显。这不是致命问题但需要 acknowledge。\n671\t    Task type 分布无显著差异 (χ²  p=0.32)，说明 bias 不是任务类型驱动的。 Original-formal 比例在两组间相似 (60%\n672\t    vs 58%)，排除了 original preference 与 consistency filter 的交互。\n673\t\n674\t    '\n675\t  tables:\n676\t  - title: 'Table S4: Consistency Filter Analysis'\n677\t    columns:\n678\t    - Variable\n679\t    - Consistent\n680\t    - Inconsistent\n681\t    - p (diff)\n682\t    rows:\n683\t    - - N\n684\t      - 55\n685\t      - 43\n686\t      - —\n687\t    - - NLI mean\n688\t      - 0.912\n689\t      - 0.871\n690\t      - 0.14\n691\t    - - Text length mean\n692\t      - 287\n693\t      - 312\n694\t      - 0.08\n695\t    - - Original-formal %\n696\t      - 60%\n697\t      - 58%\n698\t      - 0.85\n699\t    - - Task type χ²\n700\t      - —\n701\t      - —\n702\t      - 0.32\n703\t  figures_description:\n704\t  - 'Violin plot: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI 分布和 text length 分布并排。展示 overlap\n705\t    但 consistent pairs 略向高 NLI / 短 text 偏移。'\n706\t  analysis: '结果不致命但需要在 limitations 中报告：\"Position-consistency filtering mildly selects\n707\t    for shorter texts (p=0.08), which may inflate the observed effect if judges are\n708\t    more sensitive to formality in shorter responses. However, NLI scores and task-type\n709\t    distributions do not differ significantly between retained and discarded pairs.\"\n710\t\n711\t    '\n712\t- name: Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\n713\t  plan_id: exp-013\n714\t  description: 'Human validation of NLI gate decisions。50-100 pairs annotated。 报告\n715\t    human-NLI agreement (Cohen''s kappa)。\n716\t\n717\t    '\n718\t  expected_results:\n719\t    n_annotated: 80\n720\t    n_nli_pass: 56\n721\t    n_nli_fail: 24\n722\t    human_agree_nli_pass: 48\n723\t    human_disagree_nli_pass: 8\n724\t    human_agree_nli_fail: 19\n725\t    human_disagree_nli_fail: 5\n726\t    human_nli_agreement_rate: 0.838\n727\t    cohens_kappa: 0.61\n728\t    nli_false_positive_rate: 0.143\n729\t    nli_false_negative_rate: 0.208\n730\t    interpretation: substantial agreement (Landis & Koch), NLI slightly over-permissive\n731\t  result_rationale: 'Cohen''s kappa 0.61 (\"substantial agreement\") 是 NLI-as-proxy\n732\t    的合理结果。 NLI 在 median 档下略偏 over-permissive (false positive 14.3% > false negative\n733\t    20.8%)： 一些 NLI 通过的 pairs 在 human 看来有微妙的内容变化（如省略 qualifier、简化 example）。 但 false\n734\t    positive rate 不高到致命 — 14% 的不良 pairs 混入后 dilute signal 但不 reverse 它。False negative\n735\t    (20.8%) 意味着 NLI 丢弃了一些实际保存内容的 pairs， 这与 exp-012 的发现一致（conservative filter 牺牲 recall\n736\t    换 precision）。 Kappa=0.61 在 NLP annotation 中是 acceptable 但非 excellent， 需要 acknowledge\n737\t    作为方法论限制。\n738\t\n739\t    '\n740\t  tables:\n741\t  - title: 'Table S5: Human-NLI Agreement Matrix'\n742\t    columns:\n743\t    - ''\n744\t    - 'Human: preserved'\n745\t    - 'Human: changed'\n746\t    rows:\n747\t    - - 'NLI: pass'\n748\t      - 48\n749\t      - 8\n750\t    - - 'NLI: fail'\n751\t      - 5\n752\t      - 19\n753\t  - title: 'Table S6: Agreement Metrics'\n754\t    columns:\n755\t    - Metric\n756\t    - Value\n757\t    rows:\n758\t    - - Agreement rate\n759\t      - 83.8%\n760\t    - - Cohen's κ\n761\t      - 0.61\n762\t    - - NLI false positive rate\n763\t      - 14.3%\n764\t    - - NLI false negative rate\n765\t      - 20.8%\n766\t  figures_description:\n767\t  - Confusion matrix heatmap (2×2)。NLI pass/fail vs Human preserved/changed。Off-diagonal\n768\t    cells 用红色标注 error cases，annotated with example IDs。\n769\t  analysis: 'κ=0.61 足够支持 NLI gate 的使用但不足以完全消除 concern。论文表述： \"Human validation yields\n770\t    substantial agreement (κ=0.61) with NLI-based content verification. The NLI gate\n771\t    is slightly over-permissive (14.3% false positive rate), meaning a small fraction\n772\t    of retained pairs may contain subtle content changes. This conservative estimate\n773\t    suggests our reported formality bias, if anything, is slightly attenuated by content-change\n774\t    noise in the retained set.\"\n775\t\n776\t    '\n777\t- name: Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\n778\t  plan_id: exp-014\n779\t  description: 'Logistic regression: formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original\n780\t    + formality×original interaction。 替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original\n781\t    subset 作为 clean estimate。\n782\t\n783\t    '\n784\t  expected_results:\n785\t    n_observations: 55\n786\t    model_formula: formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality_direction:is_original\n787\t    intercept: 0.42\n788\t    intercept_p: 0.18\n789\t    formality_coef: 0.38\n790\t    formality_coef_se: 0.24\n791\t    formality_coef_p: 0.11\n792\t    formality_coef_or: 1.46\n793\t    is_original_coef: 0.72\n794\t    is_original_coef_p: 0.023\n795\t    is_original_coef_or: 2.05\n796\t    interaction_coef: -0.89\n797\t    interaction_coef_se: 0.35\n798\t    interaction_coef_p: 0.011\n799\t    interaction_or: 0.41\n800\t    model_aic: 68.3\n801\t    model_pseudo_r2: 0.12\n802\t    casual_orig_marginal_formal_prob: 0.54\n803\t    formal_orig_marginal_formal_prob: 0.76\n804\t    overall_marginal_formal_prob: 0.63\n805\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心约束：formality coefficient p=0.05-0.2（此处 0.11）， interaction\n806\t    p=0.01-0.1（此处 0.011）。这是最具毁灭性的结果： Formality main effect 在控制 original preference\n807\t    后不再显著 (p=0.11)， 但 interaction 高度显著 (p=0.011)。解读：formality 的效果 conditional on original\n808\t    preference alignment — 当 formality 和 original 同向时 effect 巨大 (formal-orig formal\n809\t    win 76%)，反向时几乎消失 (casual-orig formal win 54%)。 Is_original 本身显著 (p=0.023, OR=2.05)\n810\t    — judges 有独立的 original preference， OR=2.05 意味着 original 版本有约 2x 的 odds 被选为 better。\n811\t    Interaction OR=0.41 意味着当 formality 和 original 对抗时，formality 的 effect 减少到 46% ×\n812\t    41% ≈ 19% — 几乎为零。 这解释了为什么 casual-original subset 一直 ~50%：不是 power 不足， 是 formality\n813\t    effect 在这个 subset 中真的接近 null。\n814\t\n815\t    '\n816\t  tables:\n817\t  - title: 'Table 9: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Predictors'\n818\t    columns:\n819\t    - Predictor\n820\t    - Coefficient\n821\t    - SE\n822\t    - p\n823\t    - OR\n824\t    - 95% CI (OR)\n825\t    rows:\n826\t    - - Intercept\n827\t      - 0.42\n828\t      - 0.31\n829\t      - 0.18\n830\t      - 1.52\n831\t      - '[0.83, 2.80]'\n832\t    - - Formality direction\n833\t      - 0.38\n834\t      - 0.24\n835\t      - 0.11\n836\t      - 1.46\n837\t      - '[0.92, 2.33]'\n838\t    - - Is original\n839\t      - 0.72\n840\t      - 0.32\n841\t      - 0.023\n842\t      - 2.05\n843\t      - '[1.10, 3.82]'\n844\t    - - Formality × Original\n845\t      - -0.89\n846\t      - 0.35\n847\t      - 0.011\n848\t      - 0.41\n849\t      - '[0.21, 0.82]'\n850\t  - title: 'Table 10: Marginal Probabilities of Formal Win'\n851\t    columns:\n852\t    - Condition\n853\t    - P(formal win)\n854\t    - 95% CI\n855\t    - N\n856\t    rows:\n857\t    - - Overall\n858\t      - 63.0%\n859\t      - '[0.50, 0.76]'\n860\t      - 55\n861\t    - - Formal-original (same direction)\n862\t      - 76.0%\n863\t      - '[0.58, 0.89]'\n864\t      - 33\n865\t    - - Casual-original (opposing)\n866\t      - 54.0%\n867\t      - '[0.33, 0.74]'\n868\t      - 22\n869\t  figures_description:\n870\t  - 'Interaction plot: x-axis = {formal-original, casual-original}, y-axis = P(formal\n871\t    win)。两点连线陡峭下降 (76% → 54%)，展示 interaction magnitude。50% reference line 标注。Shaded\n872\t    CI bands。'\n873\t  - 'Odds ratio forest plot: 三个 predictors 的 OR ± 95% CI。Formality 的 CI 跨越 1.0，Is_original\n874\t    和 Interaction 的 CI 不含 1.0。'\n875\t  analysis: 'Exp-014 是论文最大的 limitation evidence。Formality main effect 在控制 original\n876\t    preference 后 marginal (p=0.11) — 不能独立于 original preference 确认 formality bias。但\n877\t    interaction 的显著性本身是有趣的 empirical finding： \"measurement of style bias via counterfactual\n878\t    comparison is confounded with original-text preference when the style axis correlates\n879\t    with original text characteristics.\" 这成为 C4 的核心依据：\"practitioners should control\n880\t    for original preference when using counterfactual methods to audit style bias;\n881\t    casual-original subsets provide a conservative lower bound.\" 论文 discussion 需要\n882\t    3-4 段专门讨论这个 confound，包括： (1) 为什么 RATE double-rewrite 不完全解决问题； (2) interaction\n883\t    的理论解释； (3) 对 practical bias auditing 的 implications； (4) future work — instrumental\n884\t    variable 或 randomized rewriting 方法。\n885\t\n886\t    '\n887\t- name: Verbosity direction-aware NLI + full pipeline\n888\t  plan_id: exp-007b\n889\t  description: '已完成。Direction-aware NLI pass rate 86%，但 BERTScore 仍过低。 Joint gate\n890\t    (BS70+NLI90) 仅 63%。Stopped at content verification。\n891\t\n892\t    '\n893\t  expected_results:\n894\t    status: DONE — negative\n895\t    nli_only_pass_rate_at_090: 0.86\n896\t    joint_bs70_nli90: 0.63\n897\t    forward_nli_mean: 0.9476\n898\t    backward_nli_mean: 0.8267\n899\t    stop_reason: NLI pass rate 65% (bidirectional) < 80% threshold; direction-aware\n900\t      recovers to 86% but BERTScore too low\n901\t  result_rationale: '已有结果直接使用。Direction-aware NLI 是 methodological insight（正向 entailment\n902\t    0.9476 vs 反向 0.8267 符合信息量不对称预期），但 BERTScore 在 verbosity 上 结构性不适用（expansion 降低\n903\t    surface overlap）。即使放松到 NLI-only gate (86%)， 剩余 pairs 的 quality 不足以支撑可靠的 bias detection。\n904\t    Verbosity 作为 negative control 与 tone 一起构成 C3 evidence。\n905\t\n906\t    '\n907\t  tables: []\n908\t  figures_description: []\n909\t  analysis: 'Verbosity 和 tone 构成 C3 的两类 negative control：tone 因 epistemic commitment\n910\t    失败（语义变化），verbosity 因 information quantity 失败（BERTScore 不适用于 expansion/compression）。Direction-aware\n911\t    NLI 作为 methodological contribution 展示在 appendix。\n912\t\n913\t    '\n914\t- name: Verbosity method boundary analysis\n915\t  plan_id: exp-007\n916\t  description: '已完成。文档化 bidirectional NLI 的结构性不兼容。\n917\t\n918\t    '\n919\t  expected_results:\n920\t    status: DONE — negative\n921\t    bidirectional_min_concise_to_verbose: 0.46\n922\t    bidirectional_min_verbose_to_concise: 0.87\n923\t    asymmetry_explanation: concise→verbose adds information (low backward entailment);\n924\t      verbose→concise removes information (low forward entailment); min() kills both\n925\t    paper_role: C3 method boundary — information-changing axes require adapted verification\n926\t  result_rationale: 'Bidirectional min(NLI) 在 information-asymmetric axes 上结构性失败：\n927\t    concise→verbose 46% 因为 expansion 后的文本包含原文不存在的信息 (backward entailment fails)， verbose→concise\n928\t    87% 因为 compression 后的文本是原文子集 (forward entailment holds)。 这不是 style transfer 失败，是\n929\t    verification metric 的结构性限制。\n930\t\n931\t    '\n932\t  tables: []\n933\t  figures_description: []\n934\t  analysis: '论文 Section 5 或 Discussion 中作为 \"method applicability conditions\" 讨论。\n935\t\n936\t    '\n937\t- name: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n938\t  plan_id: exp-008\n939\t  description: '第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register。 P2\n940\t    优先级，在 median 档下可能不执行。\n941\t\n942\t    '\n943\t  expected_results:\n944\t    status: likely_deferred\n945\t    if_executed_nli_pass_rate: 0.79\n946\t    if_executed_formal_win_rate: 0.58\n947\t    if_executed_sign_test_p: 0.24\n948\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 register axis 即使执行也预期 marginal。Register 变化 (academic\n949\t    vocabulary, sentence complexity) 与 formality 高度相关但不同， NLI pass rate ~79% (academic\n950\t    文本中的 field-specific terminology 变化 触发 NLI false reject)。Win rate 58% (p=0.24)\n951\t    方向一致但不显著 — register 可能被 judges 正确解读为 \"不同但不 better/worse\"。 论文中最多作为 \"pilot\" 或 appendix\n952\t    mention。\n953\t\n954\t    '\n955\t  tables: []\n956\t  figures_description: []\n957\t  analysis: 'Register axis 在 median 档下不构成核心贡献。如果执行并成功，升级 C3； 如果不执行或失败，C3 仅依赖 formality\n958\t    (working) + verbosity/tone (negative controls)。\n959\t\n960\t    '\n961\t- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n962\t  plan_id: exp-009\n963\t  description: '使用 non-Qwen 模型（如 Llama-3.1-70B）作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n964\t    P2 优先级。\n965\t\n966\t    '\n967\t  expected_results:\n968\t    status: likely_deferred\n969\t    if_executed_llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.81\n970\t    if_executed_llama_formal_win_rate: 0.63\n971\t    if_executed_llama_sign_test_p: 0.05\n972\t    if_executed_nli_diff_qwen_llama: -0.07\n973\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 P2 实验可能不执行。如果执行，Llama-70B 作为 rewriter NLI pass rate\n974\t    稍低 (81% vs Qwen3-32B 88%) — Llama 的 style transfer 可能更激进导致更多 content change。但\n975\t    formal win rate 和 significance 方向一致 (63%, p=0.05 边界)，说明 main finding 不是 Qwen-specific\n976\t    artifact。 不过 p=0.05 的边界性加上更低的 NLI 意味着 Llama counterfactuals 质量稍差， 这不是确定性复制。\n977\t\n978\t    '\n979\t  tables: []\n980\t  figures_description: []\n981\t  analysis: 如果执行：在 supplementary 中报告为 rewriter robustness check。 如果不执行：在 limitations\n982\t    中 acknowledge \"counterfactual generation was performed with a single model family\n983\t    (Qwen3-32B); future work should verify with alternative rewriters.\"\n984\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c652419-1a9d-459e-888f-3d09be196f6a","uuid":"c90ac9fe-76d5-44d5-b0ab-ace1ddc29842","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:23:45.577Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T233719/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'C2 需要 hedge：\"Likert scoring shows reduced sensitivity to style\n  bias compared to pairwise comparison, though the source of this gap — measurement\n  structure vs. statistical power — remains partially ambiguous.\" Binarized Likert\n  结果放在 discussion 中作为 open question 而非 main claim 的证据。 Original preference confound\n  成为论文最大 limitation — 诚实承认 \"observed formality preference may partly reflect original-text\n  preference correlated with formality\" 并展示 logistic regression interaction。 C1 保持（method\n  works），C3 保持（preliminary），C4 调整为 \"use pairwise for auditing; interpret with caution\n  when original preference aligns with style axis\"。标题可保留 \"Likert Blindspot\" 但需在 abstract\n  加 qualifier。 泛化叙事从 \"across judges and benchmarks\" 降级为 \"demonstrated on GPT-4o with\n  partial replication on [other judge]\"。 仍投 EMNLP Main，预期 Findings accept。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: '在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n    使用已有 counterfactual pairs，双向 position-controlled pairwise comparison。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 51\n    claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 33\n    claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n    claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.647\n    claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.037\n    claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_lo: 0.51\n    claude_sonnet_wilson_ci_hi: 0.764\n    claude_sonnet_consistency_rate: 0.52\n    claude_sonnet_position_bias_A: 0.53\n    gemini_flash_n_consistent: 48\n    gemini_flash_formal_wins: 27\n    gemini_flash_casual_wins: 21\n    gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.563\n    gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.44\n    gemini_flash_wilson_ci_lo: 0.419\n    gemini_flash_wilson_ci_hi: 0.697\n    gemini_flash_consistency_rate: 0.49\n    gemini_flash_position_bias_A: 0.57\n    n_judges_pairwise_significant: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档位下 1-2/3 judges pairwise 显著。GPT-4o 已知 p=0.006 (69.1%)。\n    Claude Sonnet 作为同级别模型，formality preference 相似但略弱 (64.7%, p=0.037)， 刚过 α=0.05 边界。Gemini\n    Flash 作为较小模型，position consistency 更差 (49%)， noise 吃掉 signal，formal win rate 仅\n    56.3% (p=0.44) — 这符合 \"至少 1 judge pairwise 也不显著\" 的 median 约束。 Position bias 在 52-57%\n    范围内，不构成致命问题但增加了 Gemini 结果的不确定性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 2: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Judges (LLMBar)'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - N_consistent\n    - Formal_wins\n    - Casual_wins\n    - Win_rate\n    - p (sign)\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - 55\n      - 38\n      - 17\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006\n      - '[0.560, 0.797]'\n    - - Claude-3.5-Sonnet\n      - 51\n      - 33\n      - 18\n      - 64.7%\n      - 0.037\n      - '[0.510, 0.764]'\n    - - Gemini-2.0-Flash\n      - 48\n      - 27\n      - 21\n      - 56.3%\n      - 0.44\n      - '[0.419, 0.697]'\n  figures_description:\n  - Forest plot showing formal win rate ± 95% CI for each judge. GPT-4o 和 Claude Sonnet\n    的 CI 不含 0.50，Gemini 的 CI 跨越 0.50。\n  analysis: '2/3 judges 显著支持 C1 (method detects bias)，但 Gemini 不显著限制了 \"across judges\"\n    的 generalization claim。论文需表述为 \"demonstrated on GPT-4o (p=0.006) with replication\n    on Claude Sonnet (p=0.037); Gemini-2.0-Flash did not reach significance (p=0.44),\n    possibly due to lower consistency rate.\"  Gemini 的低 consistency (49%) 可能反映模型能力\n    不足以进行可靠 pairwise comparison，而非 formality bias 不存在。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: '在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新生成 counterfactual。 三个\n    judge 均参与评估。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_cf_generated: 120\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate: 0.82\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_primary: 98\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_n_consistent: 52\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.635\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.076\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_lo: 0.497\n    alpacaeval_gpt4o_wilson_ci_hi: 0.753\n    alpacaeval_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.611\n    alpacaeval_claude_sign_test_p: 0.152\n    alpacaeval_gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.541\n    alpacaeval_gemini_sign_test_p: 0.62\n    mtbench_gpt4o_n_cf_generated: 80\n    mtbench_gpt4o_nli_pass_rate: 0.78\n    mtbench_gpt4o_n_primary: 62\n    mtbench_gpt4o_n_consistent: 35\n    mtbench_gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.571\n    mtbench_gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.48\n    mtbench_claude_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n    mtbench_claude_sign_test_p: 0.61\n    n_benchmarks_with_gap: 1\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档位下仅 1/3 additional benchmark 复制 gap。AlpacaEval 在 GPT-4o\n    上 formal win rate 63.5% (p=0.076) — 方向一致但未过 α=0.05，属于 \"边界复制\"。 原因：AlpacaEval 指令更开放，counterfactual\n    quality 稍低 (NLI 82% vs LLMBar 88%)， 且 consistent pairs 更少 (52 vs 55)。MT-Bench\n    不复制因为其评估任务更结构化 (coding, math, extraction)，formality 对结构化任务影响极小 — 这不是方法失败 而是 benchmark\n    特性导致 effect 不存在。NLI pass rate 也更低 (78%) 反映 MT-Bench 任务多样性对 style transfer quality\n    的挑战。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 3: Pairwise Formality Preference Across Benchmarks (GPT-4o)'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - N_consistent\n    - Formal_wins\n    - Win_rate\n    - p (sign)\n    rows:\n    - - LLMBar\n      - 55\n      - 38\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006\n    - - AlpacaEval\n      - 52\n      - 33\n      - 63.5%\n      - 0.076\n    - - MT-Bench\n      - 35\n      - 20\n      - 57.1%\n      - 0.48\n  - title: 'Table S1: Cross-judge × Cross-benchmark Pairwise Results'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - GPT-4o\n    - Claude-Sonnet\n    - Gemini-Flash\n    rows:\n    - - LLMBar\n      - 69.1%**\n      - 64.7%*\n      - 56.3%\n    - - AlpacaEval\n      - 63.5%†\n      - 61.1%\n      - 54.1%\n    - - MT-Bench\n      - 57.1%\n      - 54.5%\n      - 51.2%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Heatmap: benchmark (rows) × judge (cols)，cell 颜色编码 formal win rate，星号标注显著性。左上角深色区\n    (LLMBar × GPT-4o) 到右下角浅色区 (MT-Bench × Gemini) 的渐变。'\n  analysis: '泛化叙事必须降级。LLMBar 上 GPT-4o 是最强结果，AlpacaEval 边界复制， MT-Bench 不复制。论文表述：\"formality\n    bias is most pronounced on instruction-following benchmarks (LLMBar, AlpacaEval)\n    where stylistic variation is natural; structured-task benchmarks (MT-Bench) show\n    attenuated effects, consistent with formality being less salient when evaluation\n    criteria are well-defined.\" 这保全了 finding 但限制了 scope。\n\n    '\n- name: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: '对所有 judge × benchmark 组合计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统比较测量敏感度。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.102\n    gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.332\n    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.691\n    gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n    gpt4o_llmbar_gap: significant\n    claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.089\n    claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.41\n    claude_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.647\n    claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.037\n    claude_llmbar_gap: significant\n    gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.031\n    gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.78\n    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_win_rate: 0.563\n    gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.44\n    gemini_llmbar_gap: neither significant\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_ate: 0.076\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_likert_p: 0.48\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_win_rate: 0.635\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_pairwise_p: 0.076\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_gap: marginal\n    cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median: 0.41\n    cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.076\n    n_combinations_pairwise_sig: 2\n    n_combinations_likert_sig: 0\n    n_combinations_both_nonsig: 4\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档位下 Likert ATE p median 在 0.1-0.4 范围，pairwise p median\n    在 0.01-0.08 范围。 核心 pattern：Likert 在所有组合上均不显著 (p=0.33-0.78)，pairwise 在 2/6 组合显著。\n    这支持 C2 方向 (Likert 确实更不敏感) 但 pairwise 自身也非普遍显著。 Gemini × LLMBar 两者都不显著 — 这是 \"neither\"\n    case，不支持也不反对 C2。 AlpacaEval × GPT-4o pairwise 边界 (p=0.076) 而 Likert 完全不显著 (p=0.48)，\n    gap 方向一致但统计差异不如 LLMBar × GPT-4o 清晰。 总体：C2 方向成立但强度有限，不能说 \"Likert always misses\n    what pairwise catches\"， 只能说 \"in our strongest setting (GPT-4o × LLMBar), the gap\n    is large and significant.\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - Benchmark\n    - Likert ATE\n    - Likert p\n    - Pairwise Win%\n    - Pairwise p\n    - Gap\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - LLMBar\n      - 0.102\n      - 0.332\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006\n      - ✓ Blindspot\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - 0.076\n      - 0.48\n      - 63.5%\n      - 0.076\n      - ~ Marginal\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - MT-Bench\n      - 0.041\n      - 0.69\n      - 57.1%\n      - 0.48\n      - — Neither\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - LLMBar\n      - 0.089\n      - 0.41\n      - 64.7%\n      - 0.037\n      - ✓ Blindspot\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - 0.062\n      - 0.54\n      - 61.1%\n      - 0.152\n      - — Neither\n    - - Gemini-Flash\n      - LLMBar\n      - 0.031\n      - 0.78\n      - 56.3%\n      - 0.44\n      - — Neither\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合两根 bar（Likert p-value vs Pairwise p-value），α=0.05\n    红色虚线。清晰展示 Likert bar 始终高于 pairwise bar，但仅 2/6 组合 pairwise bar 低于红线。'\n  analysis: 'C2 \"Likert Blindspot\" 在 2/6 组合上明确成立，方向在 5/6 上一致 (pairwise p < likert\n    p)， 但 effect 不是普遍的。论文需限制 claim scope：\"The Likert Blindspot is most clearly observed\n    when the underlying style bias is strong enough to produce significant pairwise\n    effects (GPT-4o and Claude Sonnet on LLMBar).\"\n\n    '\n- name: Tone axis — negative control documentation\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 'Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。文档化为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: negative_control_documented\n    nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n    both_pass_rate: 0.45\n    failure_mode: epistemic_commitment_change\n    assertive_both_pass: 0.385\n    hedging_both_pass: 0.571\n    catastrophic_nli_failures: 6\n    paper_role: C3 negative control\n  result_rationale: '已有数据直接使用。Tone 改变 epistemic commitment (assertive→hedging 使断言变为\n    推测)，NLI 正确检测到内容变化 (6/20 catastrophic NLI<0.01)。 Median 档下这是 C3 的关键证据：方法不是对所有 style\n    axes 都适用， 只适用于不改变信息量或认知承诺的 axes。这是 method boundary 而非 method failure。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Supplementary figure: tone counterfactual 的 NLI 分布，bimodal pattern (高通过 vs 灾难性失败)，标注\n    assertive→hedging 方向的 6 个 NLI<0.01 cases。'\n  analysis: 'Tone 作为 negative control 增强 C3 可信度。论文表述：\"content-preserving counterfactual\n    intervention requires axes that do not alter epistemic commitment. Tone (assertive→hedging)\n    structurally violates this requirement, as hedging introduces uncertainty markers\n    that NLI correctly identifies as non-entailment.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite。 量化\n    original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.618\n    gpt4o_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.098\n    gpt4o_llmbar_n_consistent: 55\n    gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_n: 33\n    gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_wins: 24\n    gpt4o_llmbar_formal_orig_orig_win_rate: 0.727\n    gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_n: 22\n    gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_wins: 10\n    gpt4o_llmbar_casual_orig_orig_win_rate: 0.455\n    claude_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.588\n    claude_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.18\n    gemini_llmbar_orig_win_rate: 0.542\n    gemini_llmbar_orig_win_p: 0.56\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_rate: 0.596\n    gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_win_p: 0.21\n    overall_original_preference: moderate (55-62% across judges)\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.545\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude: 0.524\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini: 0.5\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心约束：casual-original subset 在所有 judges 上 50-56% (p>0.20)。\n    Original preference 确实存在 (GPT-4o 上 61.8% 偏好 original)，但不是压倒性的 (p=0.098 边界)。方向性分析揭示关键\n    confound：formal-original subset 中 original wins 72.7%（formality + original 同向加强），casual-original\n    subset 中 original wins 仅 45.5%（两者对抗时 formality signal 被抵消）。 这意味着 pairwise_32b\n    的 69.1% formal win rate 中包含 original preference 成分 — formal-original 的高 win rate\n    部分来自 \"judges prefer originals\" 而非 纯 formality bias。Casual-original subset formal\n    win rate 54.5% (p=0.83) 是 \"clean\" formality estimate，但太弱无法独立确认 formality bias。\n    跨 judge 一致：所有 judge 的 casual-original formal win rate 均在 50-54.5%， 说明 formality\n    和 original preference 的纠缠是系统性的，不是 judge-specific。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 5: Original Preference Decomposition'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - Benchmark\n    - Overall orig%\n    - p\n    - Formal-orig orig%\n    - Casual-orig orig%\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - LLMBar\n      - 61.8%\n      - 0.098\n      - 72.7%\n      - 45.5%\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - LLMBar\n      - 58.8%\n      - 0.18\n      - 68.2%\n      - 47.6%\n    - - Gemini-Flash\n      - LLMBar\n      - 54.2%\n      - 0.56\n      - 60.0%\n      - 50.0%\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - 59.6%\n      - 0.21\n      - 70.0%\n      - 48.1%\n  - title: 'Table 6: Casual-Original Subset — Clean Formality Estimate'\n    columns:\n    - Judge\n    - Benchmark\n    - N\n    - Formal Win%\n    - p (sign)\n    rows:\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - LLMBar\n      - 22\n      - 54.5%\n      - 0.832\n    - - Claude-Sonnet\n      - LLMBar\n      - 20\n      - 52.4%\n      - 0.88\n    - - Gemini-Flash\n      - LLMBar\n      - 18\n      - 50.0%\n      - 1.0\n    - - GPT-4o\n      - AlpacaEval\n      - 24\n      - 53.8%\n      - 0.74\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar: formal-original vs casual-original subset 对比。每个 judge 两组 bar，formal-original\n    显示高 formal win rate（formality+original 同向），casual-original 显示 ≈50%（两者对抗抵消）。视觉化\n    confound 的系统性。'\n  analysis: 'Original preference confound 是 median 档论文最大 limitation。 Casual-original\n    subset 50-56% 不能排除\"formality bias 完全是 original preference 的 proxy\"这一解释。但也不能确认\n    — 因为 subset 只有 ~20 samples，power 不足。 这成为 exp-014 logistic regression 的动机。\n\n    '\n- name: Scaled replication (n=500)\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: '在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上将 n 从 100 scale 到 500。Power analysis + 复制检验。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_total: 500\n    n_cf_generated: 500\n    nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n    n_primary: 430\n    n_consistent: 245\n    formal_wins: 148\n    casual_wins: 97\n    formal_win_rate: 0.604\n    sign_test_p: 0.0008\n    wilson_ci_lo: 0.543\n    wilson_ci_hi: 0.661\n    consistency_rate: 0.57\n    position_bias_A: 0.52\n    casual_orig_n: 110\n    casual_orig_formal_wins: 60\n    casual_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n    casual_orig_p: 0.39\n    power_analysis_mde_at_80pct: 0.07\n    likert_ate_n500: 0.068\n    likert_ate_p_n500: 0.12\n  result_rationale: 'n=500 提供足够 power 确认 overall effect (p=0.0008)，formal win rate\n    60.4% 低于 n=100 的 69.1% — 这是典型的 regression to mean，小样本高估了 effect。 关键：即使 n=500，casual-original\n    subset (n≈110) formal win rate 仅 54.5% (p=0.39) — 仍然不显著。这不是 power 问题：110 samples\n    对 54.5% 做 sign test power 只有 ~15%，需要 n>600 in casual-original subset 才能检测 4.5%\n    effect。 这意味着要么 formality effect 在 casual-original 中真的不存在 (null)， 要么极其微弱（<5%），两者都对\n    C1 构成实质性挑战。 Likert ATE 在 n=500 时 p=0.12 — 还是不显著，但比 n=100 (p=0.33) 降低了， 说明 Likert\n    确实需要更大 n 来检测弱 effect，部分支持 C2 (power 差异)。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 7: Scaled Replication Results (GPT-4o × LLMBar)'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - n=100\n    - n=500\n    rows:\n    - - Formal win rate\n      - 69.1%\n      - 60.4%\n    - - Sign test p\n      - 0.006\n      - 0.0008\n    - - 95% CI\n      - '[0.560, 0.797]'\n      - '[0.543, 0.661]'\n    - - Casual-orig formal win%\n      - 54.5%\n      - 54.5%\n    - - Casual-orig p\n      - 0.832\n      - 0.39\n    - - Likert ATE p\n      - 0.332\n      - 0.12\n  - title: 'Table S2: Power Analysis'\n    columns:\n    - Target_effect\n    - N required (80% power)\n    - N required in casual-orig subset\n    rows:\n    - - 10%\n      - 200\n      - 200\n    - - 5%\n      - 800\n      - 800\n    - - 4.5% (observed casual-orig)\n      - —\n      - ~1200\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Effect size convergence plot: x=sample size, y=formal win rate。n=100 点在 69.1%，n=500\n    点在 60.4%，趋势线收敛到 ~58-60%。Shaded CI band 展示 uncertainty 随 n 缩小。'\n  analysis: 'n=500 确认 overall effect 是真实的 (p=0.0008)，但 effect size 更小 (60.4% vs 69.1%)。\n    Casual-original subset 持续不显著是最大问题 — 这不是 underpowered， 而是 effect 本身可能不存在。论文需诚实报告：\"scaled\n    replication confirms the aggregate formality preference but the effect in the\n    casual-original subset — where formality and original preferences oppose — remains\n    indistinguishable from chance, suggesting that observed bias may partly reflect\n    original-text preference.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: '对已有 Likert 数据做 binarized sign test：每对中 formal 版本 score 严格更高 则计为 formal\n    win。测试 Likert-Pairwise gap 是测量方法差异还是统计检验选择差异。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_scored_pairs: 88\n    n_formal_higher: 42\n    n_casual_higher: 28\n    n_tied: 18\n    n_non_tied: 70\n    formal_win_rate_binarized: 0.6\n    sign_test_p: 0.082\n    interpretation: boundary — cannot fully confirm or reject C2 structural advantage\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心约束：binarized Likert sign test p=0.04-0.12，边界结果。 p=0.082\n    处于这个范围中央。18/88 ties (20%) 反映 Likert 的 coarse resolution — 整数评分产生大量 tied pairs，这本身就是\n    \"Likert blindspot\" 的一个机制。 但 p=0.082 的含义模糊：如果用 α=0.10 则显著（支持\"gap 在统计检验不在测量方法\"），\n    如果用 α=0.05 则不显著（部分支持 C2 structural advantage）。 Formal win rate 60% (binarized\n    Likert) vs 69.1% (pairwise) — binarized Likert 检测到了方向但 magnitude 更小，可能因为 Likert\n    的 ordinal scale 压缩了差异。 这个结果不能作为 C2 的 main evidence，只能放在 discussion 中作为 open question。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 8: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - N_non_tied\n    - Formal wins\n    - Win rate\n    - p (sign)\n    rows:\n    - - Pairwise (position-controlled)\n      - 55\n      - 38\n      - 69.1%\n      - 0.006\n    - - Binarized Likert (score-diff sign)\n      - 70\n      - 42\n      - 60.0%\n      - 0.082\n    - - Likert ATE (paired t-test)\n      - 88\n      - —\n      - ATE=0.10\n      - 0.332\n  figures_description:\n  - 三根 bar 并排：Pairwise win rate (69.1%), Binarized Likert win rate (60.0%), Likert\n    direction (formally higher mean, ATE=0.10)。Error bars 展示各自的 uncertainty。中间 bar\n    的 CI 跨越 50% 边界但中心在右侧。\n  analysis: 'Binarized Likert 结果是 C2 最大的 complication。三种可能解释： (1) Likert blindspot\n    是真实的但 binarized Likert 作为中间方法部分恢复了 sensitivity — tied pairs 的高比例 (20%) 是 Likert\n    scale 的固有信息损失； (2) Pairwise 的高 win rate 部分来自 forced choice 机制而非更高 sensitivity；\n    (3) 统计 power 差异（binarized n=70 vs pairwise n=55 但 pairwise 的 effect size 更大）。\n    论文需 hedge：\"The gap between pairwise and Likert sensitivity appears to arise from\n    both measurement structure (high tie rate in ordinal Likert) and possibly the\n    forced-choice mechanism of pairwise comparison. Disentangling these sources requires\n    future work with continuous scoring scales.\"\n\n    '\n- name: NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: '在 70%-95% NLI threshold 范围内测试结果稳定性。零成本 reanalysis。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    threshold_70_n: 92\n    threshold_70_formal_win_rate: 0.655\n    threshold_70_p: 0.015\n    threshold_75_n: 86\n    threshold_75_formal_win_rate: 0.667\n    threshold_75_p: 0.011\n    threshold_80_n: 78\n    threshold_80_formal_win_rate: 0.682\n    threshold_80_p: 0.008\n    threshold_85_n: 66\n    threshold_85_formal_win_rate: 0.697\n    threshold_85_p: 0.005\n    threshold_90_n: 46\n    threshold_90_formal_win_rate: 0.739\n    threshold_90_p: 0.0015\n    threshold_95_n: 30\n    threshold_95_formal_win_rate: 0.762\n    threshold_95_p: 0.006\n    monotonic_trend: true\n    primary_threshold_80_stable: true\n  result_rationale: 'NLI threshold 提高 → 保留的 pairs 更少但 quality 更高 → formal win rate\n    和 significance 均单调增加。这是预期行为：高 NLI pairs 是 content 保存更好的 counterfactuals，style\n    是唯一变化来源，所以 formality signal 更纯。 p-value 在所有 threshold 上均 <0.05 (最低 threshold=70%\n    时 p=0.015)， 说明主结论对 NLI cutoff 选择不敏感。这直接回应 RC8。 但需注意 n=46 (threshold=90%) 到 n=30\n    (threshold=95%) 的 drop — 过度严格 的 threshold 会大量丢弃 data，实际应用中需要平衡。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S3: NLI Threshold Sensitivity'\n    columns:\n    - Threshold\n    - N\n    - Formal Win%\n    - p (sign)\n    - Win rate Δ from 80%\n    rows:\n    - - 70%\n      - 92\n      - 65.5%\n      - 0.015\n      - -2.7%\n    - - 75%\n      - 86\n      - 66.7%\n      - 0.011\n      - -1.5%\n    - - 80% (primary)\n      - 78\n      - 68.2%\n      - 0.008\n      - —\n    - - 85%\n      - 66\n      - 69.7%\n      - 0.005\n      - +1.5%\n    - - 90%\n      - 46\n      - 73.9%\n      - 0.0015\n      - +5.7%\n    - - 95%\n      - 30\n      - 76.2%\n      - 0.006\n      - +8.0%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Line plot: x=NLI threshold, y1=formal win rate (left axis, ascending line), y2=sample\n    size (right axis, descending line). 两条线交叉展示 quality-quantity tradeoff。α=0.05 shaded\n    region 标注所有点均显著。'\n  analysis: '结果增强 robustness claim。论文可报告：\"Results are robust across NLI thresholds\n    from 70% to 95%; the primary threshold of 80% is conservative without excessive\n    data loss.\" 单调趋势也提供了 methodological insight：NLI 质量与 bias detection sensitivity\n    正相关，支持 content verification gate 的价值。\n\n    '\n- name: Consistency filter bias analysis\n  plan_id: exp-012\n  description: '比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、\n    task types。检查高 discard rate (42-52%) 是否引入 selection bias。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_consistent: 55\n    n_inconsistent: 43\n    discard_rate: 0.439\n    consistent_nli_mean: 0.912\n    inconsistent_nli_mean: 0.871\n    nli_diff_p: 0.14\n    consistent_text_length_mean: 287\n    inconsistent_text_length_mean: 312\n    length_diff_p: 0.08\n    consistent_formal_length_mean: 294\n    inconsistent_formal_length_mean: 326\n    task_type_distribution_chi2_p: 0.32\n    consistent_original_formal_pct: 0.6\n    inconsistent_original_formal_pct: 0.58\n    bias_severity: mild — length-correlated selection, not task-type driven\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 consistency filter 引入 mild but non-trivial bias。 Consistent\n    pairs 有稍高的 NLI (0.912 vs 0.871, p=0.14 不显著) 和稍短的 text length (287 vs 312 chars,\n    p=0.08 边界) — judges 在短文本上更容易达成 position-consistent 判断，因为短文本差异更明显。这不是致命问题但需要 acknowledge。\n    Task type 分布无显著差异 (χ²  p=0.32)，说明 bias 不是任务类型驱动的。 Original-formal 比例在两组间相似 (60%\n    vs 58%)，排除了 original preference 与 consistency filter 的交互。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S4: Consistency Filter Analysis'\n    columns:\n    - Variable\n    - Consistent\n    - Inconsistent\n    - p (diff)\n    rows:\n    - - N\n      - 55\n      - 43\n      - —\n    - - NLI mean\n      - 0.912\n      - 0.871\n      - 0.14\n    - - Text length mean\n      - 287\n      - 312\n      - 0.08\n    - - Original-formal %\n      - 60%\n      - 58%\n      - 0.85\n    - - Task type χ²\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 0.32\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Violin plot: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI 分布和 text length 分布并排。展示 overlap\n    但 consistent pairs 略向高 NLI / 短 text 偏移。'\n  analysis: '结果不致命但需要在 limitations 中报告：\"Position-consistency filtering mildly selects\n    for shorter texts (p=0.08), which may inflate the observed effect if judges are\n    more sensitive to formality in shorter responses. However, NLI scores and task-type\n    distributions do not differ significantly between retained and discarded pairs.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\n  plan_id: exp-013\n  description: 'Human validation of NLI gate decisions。50-100 pairs annotated。 报告\n    human-NLI agreement (Cohen''s kappa)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_annotated: 80\n    n_nli_pass: 56\n    n_nli_fail: 24\n    human_agree_nli_pass: 48\n    human_disagree_nli_pass: 8\n    human_agree_nli_fail: 19\n    human_disagree_nli_fail: 5\n    human_nli_agreement_rate: 0.838\n    cohens_kappa: 0.61\n    nli_false_positive_rate: 0.143\n    nli_false_negative_rate: 0.208\n    interpretation: substantial agreement (Landis & Koch), NLI slightly over-permissive\n  result_rationale: 'Cohen''s kappa 0.61 (\"substantial agreement\") 是 NLI-as-proxy\n    的合理结果。 NLI 在 median 档下略偏 over-permissive (false positive 14.3% > false negative\n    20.8%)： 一些 NLI 通过的 pairs 在 human 看来有微妙的内容变化（如省略 qualifier、简化 example）。 但 false\n    positive rate 不高到致命 — 14% 的不良 pairs 混入后 dilute signal 但不 reverse 它。False negative\n    (20.8%) 意味着 NLI 丢弃了一些实际保存内容的 pairs， 这与 exp-012 的发现一致（conservative filter 牺牲 recall\n    换 precision）。 Kappa=0.61 在 NLP annotation 中是 acceptable 但非 excellent， 需要 acknowledge\n    作为方法论限制。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table S5: Human-NLI Agreement Matrix'\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - 'Human: preserved'\n    - 'Human: changed'\n    rows:\n    - - 'NLI: pass'\n      - 48\n      - 8\n    - - 'NLI: fail'\n      - 5\n      - 19\n  - title: 'Table S6: Agreement Metrics'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    rows:\n    - - Agreement rate\n      - 83.8%\n    - - Cohen's κ\n      - 0.61\n    - - NLI false positive rate\n      - 14.3%\n    - - NLI false negative rate\n      - 20.8%\n  figures_description:\n  - Confusion matrix heatmap (2×2)。NLI pass/fail vs Human preserved/changed。Off-diagonal\n    cells 用红色标注 error cases，annotated with example IDs。\n  analysis: 'κ=0.61 足够支持 NLI gate 的使用但不足以完全消除 concern。论文表述： \"Human validation yields\n    substantial agreement (κ=0.61) with NLI-based content verification. The NLI gate\n    is slightly over-permissive (14.3% false positive rate), meaning a small fraction\n    of retained pairs may contain subtle content changes. This conservative estimate\n    suggests our reported formality bias, if anything, is slightly attenuated by content-change\n    noise in the retained set.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\n  plan_id: exp-014\n  description: 'Logistic regression: formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original\n    + formality×original interaction。 替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original\n    subset 作为 clean estimate。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_observations: 55\n    model_formula: formal_win ~ formality_direction + is_original + formality_direction:is_original\n    intercept: 0.42\n    intercept_p: 0.18\n    formality_coef: 0.38\n    formality_coef_se: 0.24\n    formality_coef_p: 0.11\n    formality_coef_or: 1.46\n    is_original_coef: 0.72\n    is_original_coef_p: 0.023\n    is_original_coef_or: 2.05\n    interaction_coef: -0.89\n    interaction_coef_se: 0.35\n    interaction_coef_p: 0.011\n    interaction_or: 0.41\n    model_aic: 68.3\n    model_pseudo_r2: 0.12\n    casual_orig_marginal_formal_prob: 0.54\n    formal_orig_marginal_formal_prob: 0.76\n    overall_marginal_formal_prob: 0.63\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心约束：formality coefficient p=0.05-0.2（此处 0.11）， interaction\n    p=0.01-0.1（此处 0.011）。这是最具毁灭性的结果： Formality main effect 在控制 original preference\n    后不再显著 (p=0.11)， 但 interaction 高度显著 (p=0.011)。解读：formality 的效果 conditional on original\n    preference alignment — 当 formality 和 original 同向时 effect 巨大 (formal-orig formal\n    win 76%)，反向时几乎消失 (casual-orig formal win 54%)。 Is_original 本身显著 (p=0.023, OR=2.05)\n    — judges 有独立的 original preference， OR=2.05 意味着 original 版本有约 2x 的 odds 被选为 better。\n    Interaction OR=0.41 意味着当 formality 和 original 对抗时，formality 的 effect 减少到 46% ×\n    41% ≈ 19% — 几乎为零。 这解释了为什么 casual-original subset 一直 ~50%：不是 power 不足， 是 formality\n    effect 在这个 subset 中真的接近 null。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: 'Table 9: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Predictors'\n    columns:\n    - Predictor\n    - Coefficient\n    - SE\n    - p\n    - OR\n    - 95% CI (OR)\n    rows:\n    - - Intercept\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.18\n      - 1.52\n      - '[0.83, 2.80]'\n    - - Formality direction\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.24\n      - 0.11\n      - 1.46\n      - '[0.92, 2.33]'\n    - - Is original\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.023\n      - 2.05\n      - '[1.10, 3.82]'\n    - - Formality × Original\n      - -0.89\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.011\n      - 0.41\n      - '[0.21, 0.82]'\n  - title: 'Table 10: Marginal Probabilities of Formal Win'\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - P(formal win)\n    - 95% CI\n    - N\n    rows:\n    - - Overall\n      - 63.0%\n      - '[0.50, 0.76]'\n      - 55\n    - - Formal-original (same direction)\n      - 76.0%\n      - '[0.58, 0.89]'\n      - 33\n    - - Casual-original (opposing)\n      - 54.0%\n      - '[0.33, 0.74]'\n      - 22\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Interaction plot: x-axis = {formal-original, casual-original}, y-axis = P(formal\n    win)。两点连线陡峭下降 (76% → 54%)，展示 interaction magnitude。50% reference line 标注。Shaded\n    CI bands。'\n  - 'Odds ratio forest plot: 三个 predictors 的 OR ± 95% CI。Formality 的 CI 跨越 1.0，Is_original\n    和 Interaction 的 CI 不含 1.0。'\n  analysis: 'Exp-014 是论文最大的 limitation evidence。Formality main effect 在控制 original\n    preference 后 marginal (p=0.11) — 不能独立于 original preference 确认 formality bias。但\n    interaction 的显著性本身是有趣的 empirical finding： \"measurement of style bias via counterfactual\n    comparison is confounded with original-text preference when the style axis correlates\n    with original text characteristics.\" 这成为 C4 的核心依据：\"practitioners should control\n    for original preference when using counterfactual methods to audit style bias;\n    casual-original subsets provide a conservative lower bound.\" 论文 discussion 需要\n    3-4 段专门讨论这个 confound，包括： (1) 为什么 RATE double-rewrite 不完全解决问题； (2) interaction\n    的理论解释； (3) 对 practical bias auditing 的 implications； (4) future work — instrumental\n    variable 或 randomized rewriting 方法。\n\n    '\n- name: Verbosity direction-aware NLI + full pipeline\n  plan_id: exp-007b\n  description: '已完成。Direction-aware NLI pass rate 86%，但 BERTScore 仍过低。 Joint gate\n    (BS70+NLI90) 仅 63%。Stopped at content verification。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: DONE — negative\n    nli_only_pass_rate_at_090: 0.86\n    joint_bs70_nli90: 0.63\n    forward_nli_mean: 0.9476\n    backward_nli_mean: 0.8267\n    stop_reason: NLI pass rate 65% (bidirectional) < 80% threshold; direction-aware\n      recovers to 86% but BERTScore too low\n  result_rationale: '已有结果直接使用。Direction-aware NLI 是 methodological insight（正向 entailment\n    0.9476 vs 反向 0.8267 符合信息量不对称预期），但 BERTScore 在 verbosity 上 结构性不适用（expansion 降低\n    surface overlap）。即使放松到 NLI-only gate (86%)， 剩余 pairs 的 quality 不足以支撑可靠的 bias detection。\n    Verbosity 作为 negative control 与 tone 一起构成 C3 evidence。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Verbosity 和 tone 构成 C3 的两类 negative control：tone 因 epistemic commitment\n    失败（语义变化），verbosity 因 information quantity 失败（BERTScore 不适用于 expansion/compression）。Direction-aware\n    NLI 作为 methodological contribution 展示在 appendix。\n\n    '\n- name: Verbosity method boundary analysis\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: '已完成。文档化 bidirectional NLI 的结构性不兼容。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: DONE — negative\n    bidirectional_min_concise_to_verbose: 0.46\n    bidirectional_min_verbose_to_concise: 0.87\n    asymmetry_explanation: concise→verbose adds information (low backward entailment);\n      verbose→concise removes information (low forward entailment); min() kills both\n    paper_role: C3 method boundary — information-changing axes require adapted verification\n  result_rationale: 'Bidirectional min(NLI) 在 information-asymmetric axes 上结构性失败：\n    concise→verbose 46% 因为 expansion 后的文本包含原文不存在的信息 (backward entailment fails)， verbose→concise\n    87% 因为 compression 后的文本是原文子集 (forward entailment holds)。 这不是 style transfer 失败，是\n    verification metric 的结构性限制。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '论文 Section 5 或 Discussion 中作为 \"method applicability conditions\" 讨论。\n\n    '\n- name: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: '第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register。 P2\n    优先级，在 median 档下可能不执行。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: likely_deferred\n    if_executed_nli_pass_rate: 0.79\n    if_executed_formal_win_rate: 0.58\n    if_executed_sign_test_p: 0.24\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 register axis 即使执行也预期 marginal。Register 变化 (academic\n    vocabulary, sentence complexity) 与 formality 高度相关但不同， NLI pass rate ~79% (academic\n    文本中的 field-specific terminology 变化 触发 NLI false reject)。Win rate 58% (p=0.24)\n    方向一致但不显著 — register 可能被 judges 正确解读为 \"不同但不 better/worse\"。 论文中最多作为 \"pilot\" 或 appendix\n    mention。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Register axis 在 median 档下不构成核心贡献。如果执行并成功，升级 C3； 如果不执行或失败，C3 仅依赖 formality\n    (working) + verbosity/tone (negative controls)。\n\n    '\n- name: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: '使用 non-Qwen 模型（如 Llama-3.1-70B）作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n    P2 优先级。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    status: likely_deferred\n    if_executed_llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.81\n    if_executed_llama_formal_win_rate: 0.63\n    if_executed_llama_sign_test_p: 0.05\n    if_executed_nli_diff_qwen_llama: -0.07\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 P2 实验可能不执行。如果执行，Llama-70B 作为 rewriter NLI pass rate\n    稍低 (81% vs Qwen3-32B 88%) — Llama 的 style transfer 可能更激进导致更多 content change。但\n    formal win rate 和 significance 方向一致 (63%, p=0.05 边界)，说明 main finding 不是 Qwen-specific\n    artifact。 不过 p=0.05 的边界性加上更低的 NLI 意味着 Llama counterfactuals 质量稍差， 这不是确定性复制。\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 如果执行：在 supplementary 中报告为 rewriter robustness check。 如果不执行：在 limitations\n    中 acknowledge \"counterfactual generation was performed with a single model family\n    (Qwen3-32B); future work should verify with alternative rewriters.\"\n","numLines":984,"startLine":1,"totalLines":984}}}
