{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0128pePbS49PWjpn8VEg4L5Y","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"# 项目 causal_style_decomp_judge 概况\\n\\n## 实验状态 (10 个)\\n\\n- **register_pilot**: DONE (negative) — \\n- **exp014_logistic_decomposition**: DONE (success) — \\n- **exp012_consistency_bias**: DONE (success) — \\n- **exp011_nli_sensitivity**: DONE (success) — \\n- **exp010_binarized_likert**: DONE (success) — \\n- **verbosity_32b**: DONE (negative) — \\n- **tone_pilot**: DONE (negative) — \\n- **pairwise_32b**: DONE (success) — \\n- **mvp_32b_ate**: DONE (negative) — \\n- **mvp_8b_ate**: DONE (negative) — \\n\\n## 最新报告\\n# Handover — 2026-05-21\\n\\n> 由 Agent 生成，每次状态变更后自动更新。硬限 150 行。\\n\\n## 运行中\\n（无）\\n\\n## 待处理\\n（无）\\n\\n## 近期结论\\n- **register_pilot** (negative): Register axis (academic/conversational) RATE counterfactuals preserve content (NLI+BERTScore pass rate ≥80%) and register is independent from formality (agreement ≤95%), making it a viable third axis alongside formality and verbosity\\n- **exp014_logistic_decomposition** (success): The observed 69.1% formal win rate in pairwise comparison is primarily driven by original-preference bias rather than genuine formality effect, and logistic regression decomposition will show formality coefficient is non-significant after controlling for original preference\\n- **exp012_consistency_bias** (success): The consistency filter (discarding 43% of pairs) introduces systematic selection bias by preferentially retaining pairs with higher NLI/BERTScore or different text characteristics, biasing downstream analysis\\n\\n## 趋势\\n成功 5 / 负向 5 / 失败 0 / 共 10\\n\\n## 下一步\\n（无活跃 idea，请通过 ideas.md 添加）\\n\\n## 资源状态\\nwestb-29275: 无 GPU 信息\\n\\n## 告警\\n（无）\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNjkBBkV1sbfozRh98uTph","session_id":"5c652419-1a9d-459e-888f-3d09be196f6a","uuid":"ad6998dd-8b76-4103-986c-782747981580","timestamp":"2026-05-21T00:25:06.962Z"}
