{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":431941,"duration_api_ms":614964,"num_turns":11,"result":"Review submitted.\n\n**Consensus: 3.0/6 (Weak Reject / Findings with revisions)**\n\nTop issues identified by the roundtable:\n\n1. **Self-undermined headline claim** — The logistic regression (Table 8) shows formality main effect becomes p=0.11 after controlling for original-text preference. The paper's own analysis suggests the observed \"formality bias\" may largely reflect original-text preference. Title/abstract still foreground the bias finding over the confound finding.\n\n2. **Sparse generalization** — Only 2/9 judge×benchmark cells reach significance. Directional consistency alone is weak evidence.\n\n3. **Causal overclaiming** — \"Causal style bias\" is not warranted given the confound. Should use \"interventional\" or \"counterfactual-based.\"\n\n4. **Binarized Likert underexplored** — The most novel diagnostic (Section 5.1) is shown for only 1/9 cells. Extending it is zero-cost and would clarify C2.\n\n**Key recommendation:** Reframe the primary contribution around the original-text preference confound (which is genuinely novel and has broad implications for counterfactual bias auditing methods) rather than the formality bias detection.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5c652419-1a9d-459e-888f-3d09be196f6a","total_cost_usd":2.6318974999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":56157,"cache_read_input_tokens":194026,"output_tokens":11829,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":56157,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":292,"cache_read_input_tokens":61521,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6477,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6477},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"cl